`CSSFontFeatureValuesMap.set()` throws an `InvalidAccessError` when the supplied sequence contains more values than the associated feature-value block permits.

```js
rule.characterVariant.set("alpha-2", [1, 2, 3]);
// Throws InvalidAccessError if this feature allows only two values
```

A single unsigned integer is treated as a sequence containing one value. The exact maximum depends on the feature-value block.
